  "description": "DAWBAG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C74 H88 Eu6 N8 O22 2+,2(Cl1 1-),3(C2 H6 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu1A (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2A (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3A (Eu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.518-4.012 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.99-112.41°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu6(L2)4(OH)4(MeOH)2(EtOH)2(H2O)2]·2Cl·3EtOH·H2O (C80H108N8O26Cl2Eu6; L2 = deprotonated N,N'-bis(salicylidene)(propylene-2-ol)-1,3-diamine). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
